{
  "summary": "P1 lost laptop (KB-021). User Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, Chicago) reports she left her work laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) in an Uber last night; she doesn't know if it was locked. Device status: ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:40 UTC (~09:40 Chicago), i.e. after the loss, so it is powered on and connected, possibly in a third party's hands. No warnings, 75 GB free of 512 GB. Sign-in logs (14 days): 9 sign-ins, all successful, Chicago, Duo push, normal hours, corporate/home IPs; last was 2026-10-08 13:23 UTC VPN. No failed attempts or unfamiliar locations so far. VPN access is enabled. Data that may be on it: Operations/logistics work files, cached M365 session, saved VPN profile. Actions: block_sign_in requested (pending tech approval). Still needed: remote lock now while the device is online, wipe if not recovered, revoke active sessions/tokens, and a verified password reset after the block (I haven't queued the reset yet; the user has to be verified first). The user has been asked to contact Uber lost-and-found and file a police report if it isn't returned. Side note: her mailbox is 99.4% full, low priority.",
  "reason": "KB-021 says always escalate lost devices for remote lock/wipe; ticket is P1 and the device is currently online."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for reporting this so quickly. We're treating it as urgent. Your laptop connected to our network this morning, so it's switched on somewhere. To protect your account, we've asked a technician to temporarily block sign-ins and VPN access on it. Once they approve that, any saved logins on the laptop will stop working, and you won't be able to sign in on other devices either until we reset your password. Our senior team also has your case so they can lock the laptop remotely, and wipe it if it isn't found. After we confirm it's really you, we'll reset your password and call you with the new one. Please don't share it by email. In the meantime: 1) Report the lost item in the Uber app (Help > Report an item you lost) or contact the driver. 2) If it doesn't turn up, or you think it was stolen, please file a police report. 3) Reply to tell us roughly what time you left it, the route or drop-off spot, and whether anything sensitive was saved on it outside the usual work systems. If you get the laptop back, tell us right away.",
  "internal_note": "KB-021 (P1). User: user_id 9, Mei Chen. Device BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) is ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:40 UTC. That's after the reported loss, so the device is powered on and possibly with a third party. Sign-in logs (14d): 9 successful, all Chicago, Duo push, normal hours, last one 2026-10-08 13:23 UTC (VPN). No suspicious activity so far. Account is active and VPN is enabled. Actions: block_sign_in queued (approval_id 1, pending; not done yet). Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) for remote lock now while the device is online, wipe if not recovered, and session/token revocation. Password reset not queued yet: do it after the user is verified, and deliver by phone. Asked the user for time/place details and told her to contact Uber and file a police report if needed. Side note: mailbox is 99.4% full.",
